Z||000009||Patrick's Dad||03-24-2001||09:52 PM||||Interestingly, though that came out while I was in my teens, I find much older stuff rambling on in my head. A sampling from the past week:<P>"Mack the Knife" by Bobby Darrin<BR>"Breaking Up is Hard to Do" by Neil Sedaka<BR>"I Want to Be Like You" by Louis Prima and Phil Harris (From the Disney movie, "The Jungle Book"<BR>"The Shiek of Araby" by Louis Prima<BR>"Runaround Sue" by Dion<P>I'm not sure what it's about, especially the first two. I listen to LP (and my son has The Jungle Book), and I think that Dion (Though my mother listened to him when she was a kid) was one of the great early R$R singers, I'm not a great fan of Bobby Darrin, and especially not Neil Sedaka. Oh, well. As long as it isn't Boy George, the Viiage People, or Madonna....||||reg||1
